# FIXED 2026-08-27 (the review's finding C, BUGS.md sec 17): this
# file now vets as its `expected` line says it should. Kept as the
# regression guard; the shared rows are vet-sizing-* and
# vet-must-over-a-container-* in test/spec/vet.tsv.
#
# C6 (use-case 05): a MAP-argument must() is consumed against its own
# document layer -- --canon of this file alone is {"s":{"t":integer}},
# the must() already gone: the check unified {t:integer} & {t:max(60)}
# residually, deemed itself satisfied, and discarded the bound. A peer
# arriving from the vet data document (or an @ include) is never
# checked. The schema LOOKS guarded and is not.
# expected: verdict: invalid, exit 1 with the author message "session
#           too long" (reference-language.md "Band B: must": "residuates
#           until its peer is concrete, then requires the peer to unify
#           with c"; the same two lines in one document refuse t: 120
#           with [aontu/must], exit 1)
# actual: verdict: valid, exit 0; the same pair via @ include also
#         generates {"s":{"t":120}}, exit 0.
#         CORRECTION to use-case 05's "must() is same-layer only": the
#         FIELD-level form s:{t: integer & must(max(60),"...")} DOES
#         fire across the vet meet and across @ includes (exit 1, note
#         attached -- pinned by spec row vet-must-note); only the
#         map-argument cross-field form evaporates.
# run: aontu vet must-cross-layer.aon session-120.json
s: {t: integer} & must({t: max(60)}, "session too long")
